# Documentation only; ASP.NET Core does not load .env files automatically.
# Separate App Service plans/identities. Admission: authenticated public HTTPS.
# Worker: public ingress disabled; health endpoints only, private storage/vault egress.
ASPNETCORE_HTTP_PORTS=8080
ASPNETCORE_ENVIRONMENT=Production

# Mandatory, case-sensitive: Admission or Worker. Missing/invalid fails closed.
Broker__Mode=Admission
# Missing/invalid is disabled. Durable policies control/global Enabled must also be true.
Broker__KillSwitch=true
Broker__TenantId=<single-workforce-tenant-guid>
# Entra v2 API application GUID, not api://...
Broker__Audience=<broker-api-client-id-guid>
Broker__ManagedIdentityClientId=<this-process-user-assigned-managed-identity-client-id-guid>
Broker__StorageAccountName=<private-storage-account-name>
Broker__OperationsTableName=operations
Broker__PolicyTableName=policies
Broker__QueueName=maintenance
Broker__PoisonQueueName=maintenance-poison

# Worker ONLY: omit both on Admission. Never configure credentials/shared keys.
# Broker__GitHubAppId=<positive-numeric-github-app-id>
# Broker__KeyVaultKeyUri=https://<vault>.vault.azure.net/keys/<key>/<32-hex-pinned-version>

# No static capability/principal arrays. Bootstrap owns the policy table.
# Seed contract (property names/case and Azure Table types are exact):
# PK=control RK=global: Enabled Edm.Boolean.
# PK=capability RK=<capabilityId>: Enabled Edm.Boolean; Version, RepositoryId,
# InstallationId Edm.Int64; Owner, Name, BaseBranch Edm.String.
# PK=principal:<lowercase SHA256 UTF-8 "Mode|tenant|oid|azp"> RK=<capabilityId>:
# Enabled Edm.Boolean; Version (grant version), CapabilityVersion, RepositoryId,
# InstallationId Edm.Int64; Mode, TenantId, ObjectId, ClientId, Owner, Name,
# BaseBranch Edm.String. Mode is Workload|Delegated; all GUID strings lowercase D.
# The grant's full repository binding must equal the capability row; CapabilityVersion
# must equal its Version. Admin must increment versions for changes/re-enablement.
# REST Int64 values require type annotations and quoted decimal strings, for example:
# "Version@odata.type": "Edm.Int64", "Version": "1"
# Identity GUIDs are Edm.String, NOT Edm.Guid. Enabled is a JSON Boolean.
# Bootstrap creates tables/queues; no runtime CreateIfNotExists or policy writes.
# Both runtime identities: policy entity READ only. No Graph permissions.
# Admission: operation/outbox table read/write; maintenance queue Message Sender only.
# Admission readiness checks policy + operations tables only; it does not access queues.
# Outbox dispatch runs in Worker, so Admission does not need queue metadata/dequeue access.
# Worker: operation/outbox/budget table read/write; queue send/receive/delete,
# poison send/properties read, pinned Key Vault keys/read + keys/sign/action only.
# Worker readiness also reads properties of both queues, but never dequeues or sends.
# Scope table Contributor to operations and Reader to policies, never account-wide.
# Fixed budgets: 1 concurrent operation and 6 starts/hour per installation.
# Decisions expire at min(original JWT exp, acceptance + 5 minutes), for both modes.
# Fixed worker deadline 90s, ownership 120s (capped by decision), queue invisibility 150s.
# Idempotency records are retained indefinitely. No automatic operation deletion.
# Only dispatched outbox rows are removed; poison messages have infinite TTL.
# Queue bodies contain only "<capabilityId>.<64-lowercase-hex-operation-hash>".
# Stale Working/Reconciling never resumes writes; read-only PR reconciliation only.
# If authority expired/revoked or reconciliation is inconclusive: reconciliation_required.
# There is no exactly-once guarantee or atomic fence between Azure and GitHub.
# Worker trusts decisions in the operations table written by trusted Admission.
# Revocation/lease loss can race an already issued external request. A crashed worker
# may leave an installation token alive until expiry; unknown/lost token responses
# cannot be revoked. Known tokens always get an independent bounded revocation attempt.
# Network isolation, managed-identity RBAC, HTTPS-only ingress and clock sync are
# deployment requirements; application code does not provision or verify those.
